  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...Temperatures of near to \naround 5 degrees below normal will persist through the long-term \nperiod. Sunday will warm a few degrees compared to Saturday, as our \narea gets a brief period of southwesterly return flow ahead of the \nnext system. Consensus is still good on another cold front, weaker \nthan that of Friday, crossing over our area come late Sunday. This \nfront will help keep breezy west/northwest winds and the cool \nconditions in place. This trough should keep the tropical moisture \nfrom activity in the eastern Pacific south and east of our area. \nHowever, guidance has trended a little wetter with this front, \nsupporting a 15-30% chance of showers primarily across higher \nterrain of southwest Idaho. Although uncertainty is still on the \nhigher side in regard to moisture availability.  Shortwave ridging \nbehind this trough will for dry conditions and a warming trend into \nmid-week next week.",
